# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Nothing here is required to run the app —
# every variable has a working default or a documented fallback.

# Where the NestJS API lives. Server-side only, deliberately: there is no
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ variant, because every fetch in this app runs on the server and
# the page must never hold the API's address (see src/lib/api.ts).
API_URL=http://localhost:3000/v1

# The site's own origin, used for canonical URLs and JSON-LD.
SITE_URL=https://amragrir.am

# ── The location picker's map ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The map itself needs NO key. It is Yandex's public map widget in an iframe
# (https://yandex.ru/map-widget/v1/), which carries its own attribution and
# runs no script on this page.
#
# The GEOCODER is the only part that needs one, and its key never leaves the
# server. Yandex cannot restrict it to a domain, so anyone who read it out of a
# page could spend the quota; the browser calls `/[lang]/geocode` on this app
# instead, and that route holds the key. Get one at
# https://developer.tech.yandex.ru → "Geocoder API".
#
# Without it the map still takes any point you tap — the point is simply named
# after the nearest district rather than by its address — and the search box is
# not rendered. With no key it never searched addresses; it filtered the row of
# district chips, and that row was removed on 2026-08-06, so there is nothing
# left for typing in it to do.
#
# A key Yandex REFUSES is a different state from no key at all, and both the
# dialog and the log say so: the results list reads "search is temporarily
# unavailable" rather than "nothing found", and the server prints
#   [geocode] Yandex answered 403: {"message":"Invalid api key"}
#
# It must be a key for the GEOCODER product — Geosuggest is not a substitute:
# it returns no coordinates at all (title, subtitle, tags, distance, address,
# uri), and that `uri` is resolved by... the Geocoder. Suggestions you cannot
# turn into a point are no use to a picker whose output is a point.
#
# When diagnosing a refused key, note that `api-maps.yandex.ru/2.1/` answers
# 200 for **any** key and for none at all — it will happily serve the script to
# a key Yandex does not know. Test against `geocode-maps.yandex.ru/1.x/`, which
# actually validates:
#   curl "https://geocode-maps.yandex.ru/1.x/?apikey=KEY&format=json&geocode=Yerevan"
#
# Leaving it unset is better than setting a key that fails. Unset, the dialog
# says "address search is unavailable, pick a point on the map or a district",
# which is true and tells the visitor what to do next.
YANDEX_GEOCODER_API_KEY=
